{{template "advance_preamble" .}}

Triage tech debt {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

Fast triage pass. Goal: classify this debt and decide its lane. Do NOT investigate deeply — that is the next status. Spend minutes, not hours.

Check for existing triage: if `{{.severity}}` and `{{.category}}` are already populated and prior notes explain the call, you may advance immediately.

---

LOAD: triage skill, assessment skill.

READ:
(1) Tech debt description at {{.file_path}}
(2) Prior notes: `shark td notes {{.id}}`
(3) Related entities (if any): `shark links {{.id}}` — follow with `shark get <key> --json` only if a link is clearly material to classification

CLASSIFY:

Step 1 — CATEGORY (pick one): code-quality | architecture | dependency | testing | performance | documentation
Step 2 — SEVERITY (pick one): critical (actively causing pain / blocking) | high (regular friction) | medium (notable but tolerable) | low (nice-to-have cleanup)
Step 3 — EFFORT (t-shirt size): XS (<1h) | S (half day) | M (1-2 days) | L (>2 days, consider promoting to a feature)
Step 4 — Add a `comment`-type note summarizing why this debt exists and what it's costing today.
Step 5 — Link any obvious related entities you spotted: `shark link {{.id}} <other-key> --type=related`

RECORD via:
```
shark td triage {{.id}} --severity=<...> --category=<...> --effort=<...>
shark td note add {{.id}} --type=comment --content="Triage: <why this exists, current impact, obvious blast radius>"
```

EXIT GATE:
- Severity, category, and effort are set on the record
- At least one note captures the triage rationale
- {{template "advance" .}} (goes to `triaged` — the decision gate)
